      "path": "src/domain/trade-analysis/evaluate.ts",
      "content": "`derive` still permits an omitted `valuationDate` and returns an empty `contractStatuses` array in that case; `evaluate` also still accepts that state. Removing the fallback therefore silently changes valid evaluations: a live option is reported as `Due` (because its status is undefined), and an expired option can be valued using a mark instead of returning `Unavailable(SettlementDue)`. Existing callers such as the `derivedState` helper in `evaluate-option.test.ts` still construct undated states. Retain the fallback, or make dated states mandatory and migrate all callers before removing it.",
